BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Bellissima — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261128T183000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261128T193000
DTSTAMP:20261126T213814Z
UID:bcd993e5a8f84b13198c90777d4e@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:“What is acting after all?” Maddalena (Anna Magnani) rheto
 rically asks before the mirror in Luchino Visconti’s melodrama of mother
  love and misplaced ambition. Magnani’s extraordinary performance is its
  own answer. As a working-class mother desperate to get her young daughter
  a shot at stardom through a Cinecittà casting call\, Magnani turns what 
 might have been a simplistic caricature of a domineering stage mother into
  a fully rendered character\, both hilarious and tragically human. Viscont
 i’s direction similarly refuses to distinguish between satire and sincer
 ity\; even while it mocks the business of moviemaking\, Bellissima is an e
 xquisite example of the filmmaker’s craft.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal li
 sting: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331168-film-screening-bell
 issima
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331168-film-screening-belliss
 ima
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
